<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mutapa Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mwene Mutapa state, Mutapa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mutapa Empire, also known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mwene-mutapa">Mwene Mutapa</a> state, was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shona">Shona</a> kingdom that emerged in the mid-fifteenth century between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limpopo">Limpopo</a> rivers, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a>. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nyatsimba-mutota">Nyatsimba Mutota</a>, it controlled gold, salt and trade routes linking the interior to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> coast. Weakened by Portuguese intervention and internal division, it was later overshadowed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi Empire</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwean-plateau">Zimbabwean plateau</a>.</p></div>
